{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490204,"nonce":"GzqJcd64R4uAf5kwmhKio3My+pM=","title":"Add GIC completion, hover, and signature help","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nExpose browser-neutral completion, hover, and signature-help results and connect them to Monaco. Assistance must derive from the parser, analyzer-visible declarations, built-in signatures, reserved names, and bundled GIC descriptions rather than duplicated editor metadata.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Keywords and built-ins appear in completion with concise GIC-facing descriptions.\n- [ ] Visible user functions and variables appear while out-of-scope declarations do not.\n- [ ] Reserved names are excluded where declarations are expected.\n- [ ] Hover identifies resolvable keywords, built-ins, functions, and variables without failing on incomplete source.\n- [ ] Signature help reports the active callable and parameter for built-ins and user functions.\n- [ ] Service results contain no Monaco, DOM, filesystem, or LSP types.\n- [ ] Unit tests pin service semantics and Playwright verifies each capability through Monaco.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- git-bug issue `184f8de` — Replace the browser textarea with Monaco","files":null}]}